hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18239","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated to us from Abu Ubayd the chamberlain of Sulayman from Nuaym ibn Salamah from a man of Banu Sulaym who had companionship, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished his food would say: O Allah, to You is praise, You fed and gave drink and satisfied and quenched, so to You is praise neither denied nor bidden farewell nor dispensed with."
"18476","Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Shubah informed us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani informed us, from Jurayy al-Nahdi, from a man of Banu Sulaym who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counted in his hand, or in my hand, and said: Subhan Allah is half the Scale, and praise be to Allah fills the Scale, and Allah is Greatest fills what is between heaven and earth, and purification is half of faith, and fasting is half of patience."
